<!--
  Sol y Luna: a crescent with the sun in its opening.

  The mark is the product in one shape. Two people, one in daylight and one in the middle
  of the night, on the same face — which is the whole reason the app exists.

  The crescent is **one closed path of two arcs**, not a disc with a disc removed. That
  matters. The obvious way to draw it is two circle subpaths with `fillType="evenOdd"`,
  and that is what the placeholder did — correctly, because its inner disc sat entirely
  inside the outer one, where the symmetric difference and the difference are the same
  shape. A real crescent needs the inner disc to poke out past the outer one to form the
  horns, and there even-odd fills the poking-out part as well: you get a ring with a bite
  in it and a second white shape floating beside it. Reversing the winding and switching
  to non-zero does not reliably fix it either. Two arcs meeting at the two intersection
  points is unambiguous in every renderer.

  The geometry, so the numbers are checkable rather than magic:

  - Outer circle (54,54) r22, inner circle (67,41) r22, centres 13√2 = 18.385 apart.
  - Equal radii, so they meet on the perpendicular bisector at (60.5, 47.5) ± 19.988
    along (0.707, 0.707): (74.633, 61.633) and (46.367, 33.367). Those are the horns.
  - The path runs the *major* outer arc between them (large-arc 1, sweep 1) and the
    *minor* inner arc back (large-arc 0, sweep 0).
  - Widest point of the crescent is 18.4 of 108, which survives the 24dp of a
    notification.

  Everything stays within 27.4 of centre. The safe circle allows 33 and the mask shows
  36, but filling either is a mistake this drawing already made once: at radius 30 the
  art left a violet rim two pixels wide and read as a white blob in the launcher. An
  adaptive icon needs its background to be visible as background.

  Colours are Starlight and Meridian400 from design/tokens.json, written as literals
  because the system draws a launcher icon long before any theme exists.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Crescent. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F2F2F7"
        android:pathData="M74.633,61.633 A22,22 0 1,1 46.367,33.367 A22,22 0 0,0 74.633,61.633 Z" />

    <!-- Sun, in the opening. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#F0B455"
        android:pathData="M58,41 a9,9 0 1,1 18,0 a9,9 0 1,1 -18,0 z" />
</vector>
